NAME
       fold - wrap lines to a width

SYNOPSIS
       fold [-bs] [-w WIDTH] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
       Wrap lines at WIDTH columns (default 80). Columns: a
       tab goes to the next multiple of 8, backspace goes back
       one, carriage return goes to 0; with -b every byte is
       one column. -s breaks after the last blank that fits.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

